results.answer:
Sir, I'm competent at the routine work: each evening I re-rate all 14 of your holdings, write the cut list and plan the replacements. My own nightly self-check on 30 Oct failed (plain words 38 of 39, and it knew 16 of 18 things), though 4 of 5 runs passed. I'm not yet competent at proving that my rules make money: the managed book is on session 1 of 60 and the options line on 5 of 20, so no rule has proved itself. The gaps that would make me better are:
- an early-trading signal like GIFT Nifty, and an event calendar;
- company earnings and valuation for single stocks;
- price studies on holdings outside the 250 most traded, such as Karur Vysya Bank and IEX;
- the 12 ideas that tested well but aren't in the paper rules yet, and the 36 tested only at partial scale.
